    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Nesika Beach forms the southern part of a nearly six-mile stretch of sand that extends up to Devil's Backbone.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://oregondiscovery.com/nesika-beach"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nesika Beach is known as one of the top spots in Curry County for surfperch fishing, especially from late spring to mid-summer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
        15,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://oregondiscovery.com/nesika-beach"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Beachcombers at Nesika Beach often find agates, jasper, quartz, driftwood, and shells when the tides and swells line up.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://oregondiscovery.com/nesika-beach"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Surfing is best at the south end of Nesika Beach when winds blow from the south and ocean swells arrive.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://oregondiscovery.com/nesika-beach"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Nesika Beach is located eight miles north of Gold Beach on the Oregon Coast.",
